## 15. Risks and mitigations

| Risk | Severity | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| External drag/drop behaves differently across FL Studio targets | High | Early proof of concept; test Playlist and Channel Rack separately; maintain fallback actions |
| Plugin only sees audio routed through its input | High | Explain track-level capture; require master insertion or file import for broader analysis |
| Host tempo does not provide musical key | Medium | Analyse audio or accept user metadata; never infer unsupported project data |
| Effect plugin is not a reliable MIDI instrument | Medium | Separate sampler/instrument target |
| Host resize behaviour varies | Medium | Central constrainer and repeated host testing |
| DPI/multi-monitor rendering issues | Medium | Test 100%, 125%, 150%, 200% and mixed-DPI displays |
| Real-time thread violation | High | Strict callback contract, code review and stress tests |
| Third-party analysis library licence conflict | High | Licence review before integration |
| Sample rights and generated-content restrictions | High | Track source/licence metadata and review provider terms |
| Uploading DAW audio without informed consent | High | Explicit opt-in, disclosure and privacy policy |
| Plugin identity/state changes break sessions | High | Preserve `AmE1` / `RnMu`; version state |
| Unsigned binaries trigger trust warnings | Medium | Evaluate code signing before public distribution |
| Visual effects reduce performance | Low/Medium | Cache static assets and avoid expensive per-frame effects |
| Kiro interruptions or limited credits slow development | Medium | Use Kiro only for bounded tasks; use local PowerShell, CMake and direct source review for routine work |

